  "scope": "The ORIGINAL retained residualCoefficient/kernel carrier now has BOTH signed bounds on COMMON joined eligible coprime prime intervals, including arbitrary exterior clipping and arbitrarily many phase periods. The smooth contribution is PAID: integration by parts uses the one-turning-point density exp(-t/2)*t^(j-1), retaining ZERO AND ONE orders and the full cofactor phase. Its amplitude cost is 2W/(a*abs(y)), with W the minimum of the interval amplitude bound and global factorial peak; the two-cutoff squared energy is at most b times this cost squared. Adding the ACTUAL arithmetic error gives joinedCost=smoothCost+factorialError. The exact allocation 1-boundedShare, ALL factorial orders and BOTH Riesz cutoffs remain in the literal proof. One proved but UNEVALUATED E,T works for finite radial/count families, with K=sqrt(E)*sum retainedJoinedCost. The original comparison with the signed smooth H is preserved as a stronger-information theorem. There is no count ceiling or explicit period-count multiplier, no zero or simplicity premise and no low-order deletion. The theorem requires y nonzero; the sharper arithmetic threshold is eventual, not asserted at 5000. Actual prime holes, unique ownership/incidence accounting and the TOTAL source-scaled cost remain OPEN. Never append credits already included in complete intervals. This new budget is NOT uniformly better than the earlier joined-period bound; the numerical comparison improves long intervals but loses on some short intervals. The all-order binomial-cap source budget still grows at large N; this is a diagnostic of that positive budget, not a carrier lower bound or a proved asymptotic no-go. Both whole -79/1000 floor and 3/2 ceiling remain open; no zero exclusion or RH claim. Probes are optional floating diagnostics, never CI certificates.",
